From: Bert Belder <bertbelder@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: Add Isolate::CollectGarbageForExternalMemory

An embedder that reports memory V8 cannot see has no public way to ask for
one plain major collection. MemoryPressureNotification(kCritical) is the only
level V8 acts on when incremental marking is disabled, but it is a near-OOM
path: CheckMemoryPressure() first clears the compilation cache and the
serializer data, aborts concurrent optimization jobs, flushes Liftoff code and
releases the pooled pages of every isolate in the group, and
CollectGarbageOnMemoryPressure() then runs a second collection whenever
committed-minus-live plus the reported external total is over 8 MB and a tenth
of committed, which for a small heap it almost always is.

This exposes the collection on its own: one full mark-compact with
GCFlag::kNoFlags, attributed to kExternalMemoryPressure, which runs the
embedder's weak callbacks and so lets what the embedder reported be freed, and
leaves V8's caches and page pools alone.

diff --git a/include/v8-isolate.h b/include/v8-isolate.h
--- a/include/v8-isolate.h
+++ b/include/v8-isolate.h
@@ -1177,6 +1177,20 @@
    */
   int64_t AdjustAmountOfExternalAllocatedMemoryImpl(int64_t change_in_bytes);
 
+  /**
+   * Performs one full garbage collection, so that memory the embedder has
+   * reported through AdjustAmountOfExternalAllocatedMemoryImpl() and holds
+   * until a weak callback runs can be freed. Unlike
+   * MemoryPressureNotification(MemoryPressureLevel::kCritical) it collects
+   * once and leaves the compilation cache, the serializer data, concurrent
+   * optimization jobs and the isolate group's page pools alone; unlike
+   * LowMemoryNotification() it does not collect repeatedly until the root set
+   * is stable. Intended for an embedder that has disabled incremental
+   * marking, for which V8 does not act on reported memory on its own. The
+   * isolate must be entered and locked by the calling thread.
+   */
+  void CollectGarbageForExternalMemory();
+
   /**
    * Returns heap profiler for this isolate. Will return NULL until the isolate
    * is initialized.
diff --git a/src/api/api.cc b/src/api/api.cc
--- a/src/api/api.cc
+++ b/src/api/api.cc
@@ -9892,7 +9892,14 @@
   i::Isolate* i_isolate = reinterpret_cast<i::Isolate*>(this);
   return i_isolate->heap()->UpdateExternalMemory(change_in_bytes);
 }
 
+void Isolate::CollectGarbageForExternalMemory() {
+  DCHECK_EQ(this, Isolate::TryGetCurrent());
+  i::Isolate* i_isolate = reinterpret_cast<i::Isolate*>(this);
+  i_isolate->heap()->CollectAllGarbage(
+      i::GCFlag::kNoFlags, i::GarbageCollectionReason::kExternalMemoryPressure);
+}
